4	/**
5	 * Shared network guard for the public "free tools" API routes.
6	 *
7	 * Every network tool that reaches out to a user-supplied host MUST route through
8	 * `resolvePublicHost()` (or at least `isBlockedIp()`), so an attacker can't turn
9	 * our server into an SSRF proxy for internal services, cloud metadata endpoints,
10	 * or the loopback interface. We resolve the hostname ourselves and reject if ANY
11	 * resolved address falls in a private / loopback / link-local / reserved range —
12	 * closing the DNS-rebinding hole where a name resolves public on first lookup and
13	 * private on the connect.
